<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sittaung River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sittang River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sittaung is a river of central and southern Myanmar, flowing south for about 420 km between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Bago</a> Yoma hills and the Shan Plateau into the Gulf of Martaban. The town of Toungoo on its middle course was the cradle of the Toungoo dynasty. In February 1942 British and Indian troops retreating from the Japanese suffered heavy losses when the Sittang bridge was blown up with many of them still on the far bank.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sittaung-river.jpg" alt="Sittaung River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ericwinny · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sittaung_River.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
